From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:21:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 115/116] =?UTF-8?q?ChopGimp:=20filter=20dialogs=20as=20Pho?=
 =?UTF-8?q?toshop's,=20unified=20=C2=AB=20Style=20de=20calque=20=C2=BB=20w?=
 =?UTF-8?q?indow=20(lot=20B)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Tool and filter dialogs: no header bar, buttons at the bottom
  (Réinitialiser on the left, Annuler and Valider on the right, Valider as
  the suggested action; Enter = Valider, Esc = Annuler); « Aide » becomes a
  small « ? » button in the dialog header (gimptooldialog.c, gimptoolgui.c).
- Filter dialogs: clipping, region, on-canvas controls, split view and the
  blending options in a collapsed « Avancé » expander, remembered in the
  tool options (GimpFilterOptions:advanced-expanded); preview and « apply
  directly to the layer » stay visible at the bottom.
- « Style de calque » window: when the edited filter is a layer style, a
  column at the left of the filter dialog lists the effects of the layer
  (Biseautage, Contour, Ombre interne, Lueur interne, Incrustation couleur,
  Lueur externe, Ombre portée) with check boxes (filter active). Clicking an
  effect commits the edited one without closing the window and edits the
  other in the same GimpFilterTool (gimp_operation_tool_set_operation() on
  the existing filter, as the fx list's edit); checking an absent effect
  adds it with the user's / factory defaults; « + » adds another Contour or
  Ombre portée. The session is one undo group (« Style de calque »);
  Annuler (or Ctrl+Z) undoes it and restores the active states. « Apply
  directly to the layer » is off while the window adds effects.
- New action layers-style-dialog (Calque > Style de calque > Options de
  fusion…), also behind the fx button of the Layers panel; gegl:color-overlay
  joins the ChopGimp layer styles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
